comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T19:02:02.694Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: fresh orientation, request-specific search, open/in-progress inventories and complete strict 3126-item all-status corpus found no open owner for this exact case. Full live metadata and histories of related owners confirm their completed, distinct scope. This is intake only, open and unclaimed; implementation is outside the current delivery cohort."
  "2026-10-26T22:07:04.100Z","harness:codex","Native regression initially returned assertion_failure for a genuinely absent executable. The new orchestration control now distinguishes that shell lookup failure as spawn_error while preserving exact stderr and exit status. Installed Node children deliberately exiting 127 or printing ENOENT remain assertion_failure. Platform controls cover Windows command lookup, POSIX lookup return variants, successful lookup, unavailable probes, compound syntax and expansions. Focused cohort passed 96 tests; aggregate category shape and measurement exclusion reuse existing spawn_error semantics."
  "2026-10-26T22:35:17.740Z","harness:codex","Portability refinement: Windows shell lookup can preserve either code1 or9009; recognition still requires the exact named diagnostic and an actual negative lookup. The native regression now compares both exit status and stderr directly with an independently spawned platform shell, avoiding an assumed Windows code. Microsoft Terminal documents9009 for a command lookup failure: https://github.com/microsoft/terminal/wiki/Frequently-Asked-Questions-(FAQ)/cac7ddd81f2016142f41313cf459f3a1a2efc773 . Mocked platform controls include both statuses and installed-child negative cases. Source behavior and exact public category shape are unchanged for ordinary assertions."
  "2026-10-26T23:06:12.843Z","harness:codex",An independently installed published npm 2026.10.26 artifact reproduces assertion_failure/exit127 for the absent executable in an isolated non-Git tracker. Current public-SDK workspace consumers on both Node and Bun report spawn_error while preserving exit127. Targeted native tests independently compare exact stderr/status to a platform shell and retain deliberate installed-child exit127/ENOENT negatives. All new resolution-module branches have complete focused diagnostic coverage; canonical full-source coverage remains running.
